description.narrative:
(i) Stakeholder: by adding 34MW of capacity to the grid, the Project contributes to meeting demand growth in the Libreville area as well as improving reliability of supply. As per the utility company SociÃ©tÃ© d'Ã?nergie et d'Eau du Gabon ("SEEG"), the peak electricity demand of c. 277MW in 2019 in the Libreville area exceeds the available generating capacity of c. 239MW resulting in a supply-demand gap. Through provision of low-cost baseload capacity, the Project also contributes to reducing the cost of service; 

(ii) Environmental: The Project will generate energy from an efficient, renewable source, and thus reduce the country's GHG emissions. It also contributes to reducing the importance of thermal capacity in the generation mix, which stood at c. 68% of the capacity as of end 2019.

 (iii) Competitiveness: The successful implementation of the Project, as the country's first project-financed IPP, will have important demonstration effects.
